          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "One way to find Pythagorean triads is to do the following:",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p44-q5-demonstration-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\frac{1}{1}+\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{4}{3}\\quad\\rightarrow\\quad4^2+3^2=5^2",
              "display": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p44-q5-demonstration-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{8}{15}\\quad\\rightarrow\\quad8^2+15^2=17^2",
              "display": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p44-q5-demonstration-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{7}=\\frac{12}{35}\\quad\\rightarrow\\quad12^2+35^2=37^2",
              "display": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p44-q5-instruction",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Prove this will always generate a Pythagorean triad.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "For a positive integer $n$, $\\dfrac{1}{2n-1}+\\dfrac{1}{2n+1}=\\dfrac{4n}{4n^2-1}$. Since $(4n)^2+(4n^2-1)^2=(4n^2+1)^2$, the lengths $4n$, $4n^2-1$ and $4n^2+1$ form a Pythagorean triad.",
      "worked": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p44-q5-answer",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Let the consecutive positive odd integers be ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "2n-1",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "2n+1",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", where ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "n",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " is a positive integer.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p44-q5-answer-reciprocals",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2n-1}+\\frac{1}{2n+1}&=\\frac{(2n+1)+(2n-1)}{(2n-1)(2n+1)}\\\\&=\\frac{4n}{4n^2-1}\\end{aligned}",
                "display": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p44-q5-answer-triad-introduction",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The corresponding triad is ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "4n,\\;4n^2-1,\\;4n^2+1",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p44-q5-answer-proof",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\begin{aligned}(4n)^2+(4n^2-1)^2&=16n^2+16n^4-8n^2+1\\\\&=16n^4+8n^2+1\\\\&=(4n^2+1)^2\\end{aligned}",
                "display": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p44-q5-answer-conclusion",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "All three lengths are positive integers and satisfy Pythagoras' theorem, so this always generates a Pythagorean triad.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
